Rule 1 (images must be 4-D NHWC with positive spatial and channel dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 4 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) ≥ 1 ∧ shape(v_1, 1) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 2) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 3) > 0
>>
Rule 2 (size as tensor must be 1-D of length 2 with positive entries)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 1 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) = 2 ∧ min(v_1) > 0
>>
Rule 3 (size as list or tuple must contain exactly two positive integers)
{v_1 : list(int) ⊎ tuple(int)} |= v_1.len = 2 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, 1] : v_1[i] > 0
>>
Rule 4 (when providing size as list, images must be 4-D)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : list(int)} |= ndim(v_1) = 4 ∧ v_2.len = 2
>>
Rule 5 (when providing size as tuple, images must be 4-D)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= ndim(v_1) = 4 ∧ v_2.len = 2
>>
Rule 6 (when providing size as tensor, images must be 4-D and size must be length 2)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 4 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 1 ∧ shape(v_2, 0) = 2
>>
Rule 7 (half_pixel_centers true requires align_corners to be false)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : bool} |= if v_2 then v_1 = false
>>
Rule 8 (spatial dimensions must be positive when resizing with explicit list/tuple size)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : list(int) ⊎ tuple(int)} |= ndim(v_1) = 4 ∧ v_2.len = 2 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, 1] : v_2[i] ≥ 1 ∧ shape(v_1, 1) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 2) > 0
